---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import podcastThumb from '../assets/img/skv_podcast.jpeg';

const coachingRole = await getEntry('experience', 'skv-coaching');

const title = 'Coaching — Mira Purkrabek';
const description =
  "Eight years coaching floorball, including head coach of a Czech Superliga men's team — from an assistant role in Prague and Erasmus in Slovenia to juniors and the senior team.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Section id="top" size="text">
    <div class="coaching-hero">
      <h1>Coaching</h1>
      {
        coachingRole && (
          <p class="coaching-meta">
            {coachingRole.data.role} · {coachingRole.data.org} ·{' '}
            {coachingRole.data.displayPeriod}
          </p>
        )
      }
    </div>

    <Prose>
      <p>
        I joined Sokol Královské Vinohrady (SKV) in 2017 as an assistant to the
        men's team. Along the way, I coached in Slovenia during Erasmus, led the
        SKV juniors, and returned to the men's team in the Czech Superliga. I
        became the men's head coach in 2024 at the age of 27, one of the
        youngest head coaches in Superliga history. Over that time I coached
        more than 200 matches, over 100 of them in the Superliga, and we put
        together the best results in SKV's history by building a team around
        clear roles, dedication, and team spirit.
      </p>

      <Callout>
        <p>
          In summer 2025, I stepped down from my role as head coach to focus
          fully on my computer vision research career. I remain with Sokol
          Královské Vinohrady as a consultant to the team.
        </p>
      </Callout>

      <h2 id="beginnings-in-skv">Beginnings in SKV</h2>
      <p class="coaching-meta">2017–2020</p>
      <p>
        I joined SKV in 2017 as an assistant coach for the men's team. Before
        that, I coached kids in a local club — this was my first experience at
        the highest level. I was 20, new to the club, and honestly not sure if I
        was ready. Over time, I gained more responsibility, experience, and
        confidence.
      </p>
      <p>
        In my first season with Michal Pazdera, we played in 1. liga (the
        second-highest league). We ended up winning it and earned promotion to
        the Superliga. In 2019, we managed to stay in the league by winning the
        first round of playdowns.
      </p>
      <p>
        After that second season, Michal Kotlas and David Bouša took over the
        team, and I stayed on as their assistant. That year, we finished 8th
        after the regular season and made it to the playoffs for the first time
        in SKV's history. Unfortunately, we didn't get to play them, as the
        season was cancelled due to Covid.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a
          href="https://www.idnes.cz/sport/ostatni/superliga-florbalistu-1-kolo.A180906_230419_florbal_par?setver=full"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          iDnes.cz: Vinohrady poráží Znojmo v Livesport Superlize
        </a>
      </p>

      <h2 id="erasmus-in-slovenia">A few months in Slovenia</h2>
      <p class="coaching-meta">2018–2019 · Erasmus in Ljubljana</p>
      <p>
        During my Erasmus stay, I coached FBK Olimpija for a few months and
        refereed some league matches. After returning to Prague, my next chapter
        at SKV was taking over as head coach of the juniors.
      </p>

      <h2 id="the-juniors">The Juniors</h2>
      <p class="coaching-meta">2019–2022</p>
      <p>
        In between my roles with the men's team, I coached the U19 team. I
        focused a lot on preparing players for senior floorball — not just
        technically, but mentally too. Much of that time was affected by Covid
        shutdowns, so we ran individual physical training and I mentored players
        online to help them stay connected to the sport. After Covid, in the
        2021/22 season, we qualified for the top junior league and made the
        playoffs in our very first year there.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some of the guys I coached are now part of our Superliga team. That's
        the most satisfying part of the job.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a
          href="https://www.skvflorbal.cz/c/trener-junioru-purkrabek-s-nelehkou-vyzvou-jsme-se-poprali-2033"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          SKVFlorbal.cz: Rozhovor s trenérem juniorů
        </a>
      </p>

      <h2 id="leading-the-mens-team">Leading the Men's Team</h2>
      <p class="coaching-meta">2022–2025</p>
      <p>
        In 2022, I took over the SKV men's team alongside Jan Kapucián. While
        Jan handled management and off-court matters, I was mainly in charge of
        the floorball side. We built a team from mostly young players and tried
        to play simple, hard-working floorball.
      </p>
      <p>
        In our first season together (2022/23), we finished 10th and made it
        through the pre-quarterfinal to reach the Superliga quarterfinals. In
        2023/24, we made the playoffs again from 10th place, finishing with the
        best regular-season points total in the club's history. In 2024, I
        officially became the head coach. That season (2024/25), we finished 9th
        after the regular season and reached the top 8 in the playoffs again.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm proud we've managed to make SKV a regular playoff team — even
        without big names or a big budget.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a
          href="https://florbal.cz/92593-vinohrady-prebira-dosavadni-asistent-purkrabek-kapucian-zustane-poradcem/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Florbal.cz: Purkrabek přebírá tým SKV
        </a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a
          href="https://www.skvflorbal.cz/c/miroslav-purkrabek-druha-pulka-sezony-vysledky-jsme-urvali-tymovosti-a-nasazenim-2547"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          SKVFlorbal.cz: Rozhovor s trenérem Purkrábkem
        </a>
      </p>

      <h2 id="more-than-coaching">More than Coaching</h2>
      <p>
        I hold a Czech coaching B licence and used to referee women's and youth
        games in Prague, as well as league matches during my time in Slovenia.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside the field, I'm a PhD candidate in computer vision and AI at CTU.
        I use sport as a case study in my research and have shared some of it at
        coaching seminars.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a
          href="https://www.dny.ai/event-2024/ai-4-sport"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          AI4Sports Seminar
        </a>
      </p>

      <h2 id="if-youd-like-to-know-more">If you'd like to know more…</h2>
      <p>
        We talked about some of this in a podcast for SKV (in Czech). It covers
        coaching, my view on floorball and SKV, and we even touched on how AI
        and computer vision could impact the game.
      </p>
    </Prose>

    <a
      class="podcast-card"
      href="https://www.skvflorbal.cz/c/skvely-podcast-2-miroslav-purkrabek-2430"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
    >
      <Image src={podcastThumb} alt="" width={150} height={150} />
      <div class="podcast-card__body">
        <p class="podcast-card__title">
          <span lang="cs">SKV Podcast #2 – Miroslav Purkrabek</span>{' '}
          <span class="podcast-card__lang">(in Czech)</span>
        </p>
        <p class="podcast-card__desc" lang="cs">
          Druhým hostem SKVělého podcastu byl 27letý trenér vinohradského áčka
          Miroslav Purkrabek.
        </p>
        <p class="podcast-card__source">skvflorbal.cz</p>
      </div>
    </a>

    <Prose>
      <p class="back-link"><a href="/about">← Back to /about</a></p>
    </Prose>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .coaching-hero {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .coaching-hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .coaching-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--text-subtle);
  }

  .podcast-card {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    max-width: var(--width-text);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition:
      border-color var(--dur) var(--ease),
      box-shadow var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }

  .podcast-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  }

  .podcast-card :global(img) {
    width: 96px;
    height: 96px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .podcast-card__body {
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-4) var(--space-4) 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .podcast-card__title {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .podcast-card__lang {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
  }

  .podcast-card__desc {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .podcast-card__source {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-subtle);
  }

  .back-link {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .back-link a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  @media (min-width: 480px) {
    .podcast-card :global(img) {
      width: 150px;
      height: 150px;
    }
  }
</style>
